    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Flynn Estate Agents are delighted to present Apartment 14, Block A, The Weir, a spacious and well-located two-bedroom apartment in the heart of Chapelizod village.\n\nPositioned on the first floor and extending to approximately 64 sq m / 689 sq ft, excluding the balcony, the apartment offers an excellent layout with two double bedrooms, two bathrooms, a private balcony and designated car-parking space.\n\nThe accommodation opens through an entrance hall with useful built-in storage and leads into a generous living and dining room. This is a comfortable and versatile main living space, with plenty of room for both seating and dining, while glazed doors open directly onto the private balcony.\n\nA separate kitchen adjoins the living area and is fitted with timber cabinetry, tiled flooring and splashback, together with an oven, hob and extractor fan.\n\nBoth bedrooms are good-sized doubles with fitted wardrobes. The main bedroom benefits from its own en suite shower room, while the main bathroom is located off the hallway and includes a bath with shower fitting and screen, WC and wash-hand basin.\n\nFurther features include electric heating, intercom entry and a designated parking space within the development.\n\nOne of the major attractions of Apartment 14 is its location. The Weir sits right in the centre of Chapelizod, offering the convenience of village living with the River Liffey, local cafés, pubs, shops and pharmacy all within easy walking distance. SPAR is positioned beside the entrance to the development, while the nearby Park Lane pedestrian entrance provides convenient access to the Phoenix Park.\n\nChapelizod is particularly well positioned for those looking for a village atmosphere while remaining within easy reach of Dublin city centre. Main Street is served by regular bus services, including the 24-hour Route 80 towards the city centre and Liffey Valley Shopping Centre, with additional overnight services provided by the C5 and C6.\n\nWith two double bedrooms, two bathrooms, outdoor space and designated parking in such a convenient village location, Apartment 14 will appeal to first-time buyers, owner-occupiers and those seeking a well-positioned Dublin apartment.\n\nViewing is highly recommended and is available by appointment through Flynn Estate Agents."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Living Room - 2.59m (8'6\") x 3.42m (11'3\")\nCarpeted living area with glazed doors opening onto the balcony.\n\nDining Area - 2.19m (7'2\") x 3.42m (11'3\")\nDefined dining area adjoining the living room.\n\nKitchen - 1.87m (6'2\") x 2.33m (7'8\")\nFitted timber cabinetry, tiled flooring and splashback, oven, hob and extractor.\n\nMain Bedroom - 4.04m (13'3\") x 2.92m (9'7\")\nDouble bedroom with fitted wardrobes and en suite. En Suite\n\nEnsuite - 2.28m (7'6\") x 1.51m (4'11\")\nTiled shower room with shower enclosure, WC and wash-hand basin.\n\nBedroom Two - 4.25m (13'11\") x 2.5m (8'2\")\nDouble bedroom with fitted wardrobes.\n\nMain Bathroom - 1.94m (6'4\") x 2.23m (7'4\")\nTiled bathroom with bath and shower fitting, WC and wash-hand basin.\n\nBalcony - 1.83m (6'0\") x 3.47m (11'5\")\nPrivate balcony accessed from the living and dining room.\n\nEntrance Hall - 5.62m (18'5\") x 1.09m (3'7\")\nTimber-effect flooring, an intercom entry system and useful storage.\n\nEntrance Hall - 1.97m (6'6\") x 1.59m (5'3\")\nTimber-effect flooring, an intercom entry system and useful storage."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
